Thought: I'll use batch_retrieve_polymorphs with a list of common nitride compositions. I'll include binary and ternary nitrides to get a diverse dataset.
Action: batch_retrieve_polymorphs
Action Input: {"compositions": ["AlN", "GaN", "InN", "BN", "TiN", "ZrN", "HfN", "VN", "NbN", "TaN", "CrN", "MoN", "WN", "ScN", "YN", "LaN", "SiN", "GeN", "SnN", "MgN", "CaN", "SrN", "BaN", "MnN", "FeN", "CoN", "NiN", "CuN", "ZnN", "CdN", "Li3N", "Na3N", "K3N", "Be3N2", "Mg3N2", "Ca3N2", "Sr3N2", "Ba3N2", "AlN3", "GaN3", "InN3"], "max_energy_above_hull": 0.3, "max_per_composition": 3, "save_directory": "nitride_polymorphs"}

